  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Updated to DuckDB v1.5.6\n\nNew features:\n- Typed properties for 24 DuckDB configuration options on DuckDBConnectionStringBuilder\n- Read DECIMAL values that do not fit System.Decimal as BigInteger or DuckDBDecimal\n- Bind BigInteger parameters wider than 128 bits to VARINT columns\n\nFixes:\n- Fixed possible data loss on Linux and macOS when a reader opened with CommandBehavior.CloseConnection closed the last connection to a file database (#357)\n- Errors in later chunks of a streaming result are now thrown instead of silently ending the result, in DuckDBDataReader and the Arrow stream (#356)\n- Fixed a memory leak where results skipped with NextResult were never released\n- Fixed incomplete appender rows being written with uninitialized values (#355)\n- Fixed ARRAY values shifted by one row after a NULL array in the appender\n- Fixed the appender writing to freed memory when a list of arrays grows\n- Fixed table functions returning no rows after the first iteration of a recursive CTE (#348)\n\nBehavior changes:\n- GetFieldValue<object> now returns the same value as GetValue\n- Reading a LIST or MAP into an untyped target (object, ArrayList, List<object>, or a Dictionary with object keys or values) throws InvalidCastException; use GetValue instead\n- A failed ExecuteReader with CommandBehavior.CloseConnection now closes the connection, as in Npgsql\n- Moving on from an incomplete appender row discards it and faults the appender: the next CreateRow or AppendRow throws, and rows completed before it are still written. Close, Dispose and Clear discard an incomplete row without an error\n- A blob Stream from GetStream is valid only until the reader moves to the next result set",
